case|literal value|why it is escaped
backslash|a\\b|backslash is the escape character
backtick|a\`b|would otherwise open a formula
annotation marker|a\{\{b\}\}|would otherwise open structured metadata
style marker|a\[[b\]]|would otherwise open a style
comment marker|a/\*b\*/|would otherwise open a cell comment
type-shaped text|key\:value:|would otherwise look like a type marker
date-shaped text|x\:date(2024):|would otherwise look like a parameterized type
line comment|\# tag|would otherwise be a comment line
trailing continuation|"5+"|wrapped form keeps the trailing plus literal
trailing value space|a\  :string:|escaped space precedes a type inclusion
sheet divider|"---"|wrapped form keeps an own-line divider literal
